    "description": "Forces Claude to match output scope exactly to what was requested. Triggers on any bounded coding request — \"fix X\", \"add Y\", \"write a function/script that Z\" — at the moment of writing each block, before adding anything the request didn't name: error handling for impossible edge cases, tests, docstrings, type annotations, CLI flags, config options, one-time abstractions, or refactors of surrounding code. Does NOT trigger when error handling, tests, or validation are the explicit subject of the request, or when the user asked for a complete or production-ready implementation. The best code is code you didn't write.\n",
